================================pReSeNts====================================

                              GifDesc V1.2

============================================================================
Ok... after the betatester-release(1.0a) and the quick-release(1.1) here is
GifDesc v1.2..

USAGE:
======
The usage is so simple..

-gifdesc e <source> <destination-description>

Lets assume that we have a file_id'ed gifnamed a.gif. To extract file_id 
to a file named b.diz type

        gifdesc e a.gif b.diz

-gifdesc a <source> <description>
Lets assume that we are going to add a file_id to a gif named a.gif. The 
file_id name is b.diz.So you must type

        gifdesc a a.gif b.diz

*NOTE:You can add more then one file_id's to a file. But only first file_id
will be used as a file_id. So if you want to strip all, use d parameter
of GifDesc.(will be explaned later.)

-gifdesc r <source/destination> <description>

Still we have same files.. But i would like to replace the description
with c.diz.. So type..

        gifdesc r a.gif c.diz

*NOTE:Two trunking techniques used in this part.. If the one that Commodore
put in V37 didn't work, GifDesc will open a temp file in t: So if you don't
have enough memory assign t: to harddisk.

-gifdesc d <source/destination>

To remove all file_is's only give name of the file & use parameted d.

        gifdesc d a.gif

*NOTE:Two trunking techniques used in this part.. If the one that Commodore
put in V37 didn't work, GifDesc will open a temp file in t: So if you don't
have enough memory assign t: to harddisk.

